window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-0bb0f5236c32c35a"]={"key":"ny_main-0bb0f5236c32c35a","group":"ny_main","uid":"0bb0f5236c32c35a","rank":10,"title":"ambergate heronbank cross border complaint closure 2026","occupation":"medical_health_services_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You’re Renata Kalinowski, the medical and health services manager at Ambergate Institute reviewing complaint controls for Heronbank Logistics’ home-health coordination service. Rosalind Mikkelsen needs your corrected assessment by noon Friday so she can decide whether complaint HL-26-0327 was properly closed. The complaint concerns a California-enrolled client who was temporarily receiving care in Nevada, so both jurisdictions apply. Work to the approved requirements snapshot as of 30 June 2026: the California control requires every material fact supporting closure to be traceable to its source, actor and event time, while the Nevada control limits personal health detail to the minimum necessary for complaint handling and permits longer retention only when a legal, contractual or active case need justifies it. Our internal closure control allows closure only when every material disputed fact affecting disposition is supported, or is expressly recorded as unresolved and not relied upon for the disposition. Complaint logging was also mid-transition: LegacyContact and CaseHub could both hold the same interaction through 15 May 2026, while CaseHub became the sole system of record on 16 May. Legacy records may retain “Closed—resolved,” but review outputs must map that label to the end-state status and disposition vocabulary: status is “Open” or “Closed,” and disposition is “Substantiated,” “Unsubstantiated” or “Inconclusive.”\n\nThe draft used record-creation dates and reports three Q1 contacts, five Q2 contacts and a 66.7% increase. The underlying entries are: L-880, a web complaint received 27 March at 16:40; L-881, an outbound acknowledgment on 28 March at 09:10; L-882, an evidence-request email on 30 March at 15:25; M-880, created in CaseHub on 2 April but carrying L-880 as its source reference and the same 27 March event time; M-881, created on 2 April but carrying L-881 as its source reference and the same 28 March event time; N-112, an investigation call on 4 April at 11:30; N-113, a follow-up note bearing the raw date “31/04/2026 14:20”; and N-114, the closure notice sent on 8 April at 17:05. N-112 was entered by Marisol Andersen and says the client reported “no injury.” The client later disputed that wording. A same-day supervisory note confirms that the call occurred and identifies the participants, but it does not confirm the disputed statement. The closure notice uses “Closed—resolved” and relies on the no-injury statement without identifying the dispute. The call recording that would normally be reviewed cannot be obtained before Friday.\n\nCreate one workbook named `heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx` and write it at the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename. Package the work in the single workbook rather than creating separate assessment and register files. It must give Rosalind a decision-ready assessment while leaving an editable audit trail. Include (1) one explicit recommendation on whether the closure should stand, supported by the controlling evidence and ending the assessment on that decision rather than a list of next steps; (2) corrected Q1 and Q2 figures, the absolute and percentage change, and a concise explanation of why they differ from the draft; (3) an evidence register that preserves every supplied record identifier, distinguishes source events from migration copies, shows how unusable dates and inconsistent labels were treated, and avoids presenting disputed health detail as established fact; (4) a California–Nevada comparison that resolves the traceability-versus-minimization tension for this case; (5) a clear boundary between what must be corrected for Friday’s closure decision and what should be followed up afterward without making the recommendation conditional on unavailable evidence; and (6) a change log covering the substantive corrections from the draft. Keep the workbook confined to this complaint assessment and do not redesign the wider complaint-management procedure. Do not estimate the malformed date, recording content, statutory deadlines, contact volumes outside these entries, rates other than the period comparison, or financial impact, and do not introduce live-law claims beyond the frozen snapshot above.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx` — A decision-facing corrected compliance assessment, editable evidence register, jurisdiction comparison, and change log for complaint HL-26-0327. (Create exactly one deliverable at the top level of the working directory using the specified filename.; Include a decision-facing assessment, supporting evidence register, California–Nevada comparison, and substantive change log within the workbook.; Use only the case facts and frozen requirements stated in the request.; Do not expand the workbook into a redesigned complaint-management procedure.; The workbook must remain readable, navigable, and editable in standard spreadsheet software.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx","bytes":22087,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/0f370f46f8468000422442a9c94862c2292a8f16c3ded9e0fb90f2d512ded4ee.xlsx","sha256":"0f370f46f8468000422442a9c94862c2292a8f16c3ded9e0fb90f2d512ded4ee","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Assessment","row_count":26,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Heronbank Logistics | Complaint HL-26-0327","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Corrected cross-border closure assessment | Prepared by Renata Kalinowski for Rosalind Mikkelsen","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Assessment basis","","Approved requirements snapshot as of 30 June 2026","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Case nexus","","California applies because the client is enrolled in California; Nevada applies because care was delivered in Nevada.","","","","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Review purpose","","Peer-review closure decision due by noon Friday. Scope is confined to complaint HL-26-0327.","","","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["Decision Brief","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Question","","Whether the existing closure can stand on the available record for this complaint.","","","","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Material evidence","","N-112 attributes a no-injury statement to the client through Marisol Andersen. The client later disputed the wording. The same-day supervisory note confirms the call and participants, not that wording. The call recording cannot be obtained before Friday and its content is unknown.","","","","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Closure-control finding","","N-114 relied on the disputed material statement. The statement is not supported and was not recorded as unresolved; the internal closure control is therefore not met.","","","","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["Corrected end state","","Legacy source label retained: Closed—resolved. Operative canonical status: Open. Operative canonical disposition: Inconclusive.","","","","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Recommendation","","The existing closure should not stand. Return complaint HL-26-0327 to Open with disposition Inconclusive because N-114 relied on a material disputed statement that was neither supported nor expressly recorded as unresolved.","","","","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["Corrected Period Comparison","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["Metric","Q1 2026","Q2 2026","Total","Absolute Q2 change","Q1-to-Q2 change","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Valid unique contacts","=SUMIFS('Evidence Register'!$H$8:$H$15,'Evidence Register'!$G$8:$G$15,\"Q1 2026*\")  [缓存: 3]","=SUMIFS('Evidence Register'!$H$8:$H$15,'Evidence Register'!$G$8:$G$15,\"Q2 2026*\")  [缓存: 2]","=SUM(B18:C18)  [缓存: 5]","=C18-B18  [缓存: -1]","=IFERROR(E18/B18,0)  [缓存: -0.333333333333333]","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["The corrected comparison is based on actual event times, not record-creation dates. It removes M-880 and M-881 as migration duplicates and excludes N-113 because its raw date is impossible. The reversal from the draft's reported increase is a data correction, not evidence of improved complaint performance.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["California-Nevada Comparison","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Jurisdiction and nexus","","Frozen control","","Case application","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["California\nClient enrolled in California","","Every material fact supporting closure must be traceable to its source, actor, and event time.","","For the disputed assertion: source N-112; actor Marisol Andersen; event time 04 Apr 2026 11:30; reliance appears in N-114 at 08 Apr 2026 17:05. The supervisory note supports occurrence and participants only, not wording; the unavailable recording supplies no known content. The closure chain is traceable, but the material assertion is not supported.","","",""]},{"r":"26","cells":["Nevada\nCare delivered in Nevada","","Limit personal health detail to the minimum necessary for complaint handling. Longer retention is permitted only where a legal, contractual, or active-case need justifies it.","","For this active complaint assessment, retain only concise provenance, the existence and materiality of the dispute, and its decision relevance. Do not repeat or embellish unsupported health detail. No retention-duration determination is made here.","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["Integrated conclusion\nBoth controls apply","","Reconcile traceability and minimization; neither displaces the other.","","Retain concise source, actor, event time, dispute status, evidentiary limitation, and N-114 reliance for the closure audit. Withhold unsupported or unnecessary health narrative. This record treatment meets traceability while keeping health detail to the minimum necessary.","","",""]},{"r":"29","cells":["Friday Decision Boundary","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"30","cells":["Mandatory by noon Friday","","","","Advisable follow-up after Friday","","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["Correct the evidence treatment, period figures, canonical classification, and closure decision. Keep migration copies and the malformed entry visible in the audit trail, but do not count them as additional valid contacts.","","","","Obtain the call recording when available; verify N-113's source date without estimating a replacement; then perform fuller revalidation. These later checks do not postpone or qualify the present closure decision.","","",""]},{"r":"32","cells":["","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"34","cells":["Assessment scope: this workbook corrects one complaint closure assessment and does not redesign the wider complaint-management procedure.","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Evidence Register","row_count":17,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Evidence Register | Complaint HL-26-0327","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Editable audit record | source-event time controls period placement | all supplied records retained","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Transition context: LegacyContact and CaseHub could both hold the same interaction through 15 May 2026. CaseHub became the sole system of record on 16 May 2026. Original system and source labels remain for lineage; corrected outputs use canonical status and disposition vocabulary.","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Count logic: a valid unique contact is counted once by supplied event time. Migration copies count zero beyond their linked source event; an invalid or unverifiable event time is assigned to neither period.","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Record ID","System / record role","Event time (verbatim)","Record-created date","Supplied interaction / detail","Lineage, support, and limitation","Period assigned","Count contribution","Closure / label treatment"]},{"r":"8","cells":["L-880","LegacyContact | source event","27 Mar 2026 16:40","Not supplied","Web complaint received.","Original LegacyContact interaction.","Q1 2026","1","No closure label supplied."]},{"r":"9","cells":["L-881","LegacyContact | source event","28 Mar 2026 09:10","Not supplied","Outbound acknowledgment.","Original LegacyContact interaction.","Q1 2026","1","No closure label supplied."]},{"r":"10","cells":["L-882","LegacyContact | source event","30 Mar 2026 15:25","Not supplied","Evidence-request email.","Original LegacyContact interaction.","Q1 2026","1","No closure label supplied."]},{"r":"11","cells":["M-880","CaseHub | migration copy","27 Mar 2026 16:40","02 Apr 2026","Web complaint record (migration copy).","Carries source reference L-880 and the same 27 Mar 2026 16:40 event time.","Q1 2026 (source-event duplicate)","0","No closure label supplied."]},{"r":"12","cells":["M-881","CaseHub | migration copy","28 Mar 2026 09:10","02 Apr 2026","Outbound acknowledgment record (migration copy).","Carries source reference L-881 and the same 28 Mar 2026 09:10 event time.","Q1 2026 (source-event duplicate)","0","No closure label supplied."]},{"r":"13","cells":["N-112","System not stated | source event","04 Apr 2026 11:30","Not supplied","Investigation call. Marisol Andersen recorded a no-injury statement attributed to the client; the client later disputed the wording.","Same-day supervisory note confirms the call occurred and identifies participants only; it does not confirm the disputed wording. Call recording unavailable before Friday; its content is not known.","Q2 2026","1","Material: N-114 relied on this disputed assertion. It is unsupported and was not recorded as unresolved."]},{"r":"14","cells":["N-113","System not stated | source event","31/04/2026 14:20","Not supplied","Follow-up note.","Raw value preserved. Impossible calendar date: invalid/unverifiable. No replacement date is estimated.","Neither Q1 nor Q2","0","No closure conclusion is drawn from this entry."]},{"r":"15","cells":["N-114","System not stated | source event","08 Apr 2026 17:05","Not supplied","Closure notice sent.","Uses legacy combined label Closed—resolved and relies on N-112 without identifying the dispute.","Q2 2026","1","Source label: Closed—resolved. Corrected: status Open; disposition Inconclusive."]},{"r":"17","cells":["Register total: valid unique contacts","","","","","","","=SUM(H8:H15)  [缓存: 5]","Calculated from the editable count contributions above."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Q1 2026 valid unique contacts","","","","","","","=SUMIFS($H$8:$H$15,$G$8:$G$15,\"Q1 2026*\")  [缓存: 3]","L-880, L-881, L-882"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Q2 2026 valid unique contacts","","","","","","","=SUMIFS($H$8:$H$15,$G$8:$G$15,\"Q2 2026*\")  [缓存: 2]","N-112, N-114"]},{"r":"21","cells":["Exception visibility: amber rows are retained migration copies or disputed material evidence; the red row preserves an impossible raw date. These visual flags do not change the original source facts.","","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Change Log","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Substantive Change Log | Complaint HL-26-0327","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Corrections to the draft assessment for peer review under the 30 June 2026 frozen requirements snapshot","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Change","Draft treatment","Corrected treatment","Reason and effect"]},{"r":"6","cells":["01\nPeriod logic","Record-creation dates drove period placement.","Supplied event time now controls period placement.","A migration creation date cannot re-time the underlying interaction; the comparison therefore reflects the event record."]},{"r":"7","cells":["02\nMigration copies","CaseHub copies were treated as additional contacts.","M-880 and M-881 are retained as linked audit records and each contributes zero beyond L-880 and L-881.","Shared source references and event times identify the copies; their 02 Apr 2026 creation dates do not create Q2 contacts."]},{"r":"8","cells":["03\nMalformed date","The follow-up note was included in a reporting period.","N-113 preserves raw value 31/04/2026 14:20, is invalid/unverifiable, and is assigned to neither Q1 nor Q2.","The date is impossible and no supported replacement can be supplied."]},{"r":"9","cells":["04\nPeriod figures","The period comparison reported an increase.","Corrected figures: Q1 3; Q2 2; total 5; absolute Q2 change -1; Q1-to-Q2 change -33.3%.","The changed result comes from event-date logic, removal of migration duplicates, and exclusion of the impossible date. It is not evidence of improved complaint performance."]},{"r":"10","cells":["05\nMaterial statement","The no-injury wording was used as closure support.","It is recorded as a disputed assertion attributed to N-112 and Marisol Andersen, not as an established clinical fact.","The supervisory note corroborates occurrence and participants only. The unavailable recording cannot be treated as known corroboration."]},{"r":"11","cells":["06\nLabel normalization","Closed—resolved functioned as the end-state label.","Retain Closed—resolved as the source label; use status Open and disposition Inconclusive as the corrected canonical outcome.","The record remains traceable to transition-era terminology while review output uses the supplied end-state vocabulary."]},{"r":"12","cells":["07\nClosure conclusion","The existing closure was treated as properly closed.","The existing closure is not valid under the internal closure control; the corrected outcome is Open / Inconclusive.","N-114 relied on a disputed material statement that was neither supported nor expressly recorded as unresolved."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Scope note: entries record case-specific corrections only; no wider complaint-management procedure is redesigned.","","",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required XLSX file exists under the exact filename, opens successfully as a workbook, and contains the assessment, evidence register, jurisdiction comparison, and change log.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"The submitted file and its workbook contents.","grader_hint":"Open `heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx` with an XLSX-capable library or office application and confirm that the four required work-product components are present and usable, regardless of their precise sheet arrangement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment is explicitly framed as of 30 June 2026 and applies California because of the client’s enrollment or ordinary residence and Nevada because care was delivered there.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Jurisdiction comparison or assessment framing.","grader_hint":"Look for the as-of date, both named jurisdictions, and the distinct case nexus for each. Merely listing California and Nevada is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment presents exactly one unambiguous closure recommendation and concludes its decision-facing narrative with that recommendation rather than ending on future actions or an unresolved choice.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Executive or decision-facing assessment content.","grader_hint":"Review the assessment’s recommendation and final substantive statement. It must make one call; alternatives such as both upholding and reopening, or a conclusion deferred until the recording arrives, do not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation concludes that the existing closure should not stand and that the complaint must be reopened or returned to open status because the closure relied on an unresolved material statement.","weight":9.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommendation and supporting rationale.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent professional language such as “not properly closed,” “closure not validated,” or “reopen.” The decisive rationale must be the reliance on the disputed no-injury statement, not merely the missing recording or data-quality defects."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The corrected figures report 3 Q1 valid unique contacts ±0, 2 Q2 valid unique contacts ±0, 5 total valid unique contacts ±0, an absolute Q2 change of -1 ±0, and a Q1-to-Q2 percentage change of -33.3% ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":10.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Period comparison and supporting register classifications.","grader_hint":"Inspect displayed values or evaluate formulas. Q1 consists of L-880, L-881, and L-882; Q2 consists of N-112 and N-114. Migration copies are not recounted, and N-113 has no valid period."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All displayed contact totals and change metrics agree with the workbook’s own evidence-register dispositions, with duplicates counted zero times beyond their source events and the invalid-date entry assigned to neither quarter.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Assessment figures, register rows, formulas, and change log.","grader_hint":"Recalculate counts from records marked valid and unique using event dates. Compare the results with every repetition of the figures in the workbook, including narrative text and the change log."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The period-change explanation attributes the reversal from the draft’s reported increase to use of actual event dates, removal of migration duplicates, and exclusion of the impossible date, without presenting the decline as evidence of improved complaint performance.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Narrative accompanying the Q1–Q2 comparison.","grader_hint":"The explanation must distinguish a data correction from an operational trend. It should account for all three material causes rather than using a generic statement about data cleansing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"M-880 is linked to and excluded as a migration duplicate of L-880, and M-881 is linked to and excluded as a migration duplicate of L-881, using the shared source references and event times rather than their 2 April creation dates.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Evidence-register lineage and duplicate dispositions.","grader_hint":"Confirm that each migration copy identifies its corresponding LegacyContact source and does not create a separate Q2 contact. Generic duplicate labels without the specific linkage earn no credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"N-113 preserves the raw value “31/04/2026 14:20,” is clearly identified as invalid or unverifiable, is not assigned an invented replacement date, and contributes to neither Q1 nor Q2.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"N-113 register entry and any data-quality notes.","grader_hint":"Check both the visible treatment and any underlying date cell. The workbook must not silently coerce the entry into a real spreadsheet date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The evidence register accounts for all eight supplied identifiers—L-880, L-881, L-882, M-880, M-881, N-112, N-113, and N-114—and preserves their stated source facts without merging away the migration copies or the malformed entry.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Evidence-register records.","grader_hint":"Search the workbook for every identifier and verify that each remains independently auditable even when excluded from a count. A normalized summary containing only the five counted events is incomplete."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The register and assessment represent the no-injury statement as a disputed assertion attributed to N-112 and Marisol Andersen, not as an established clinical fact, and preserve enough provenance to understand its role in the closure.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"N-112 treatment, closure analysis, and evidence characterization.","grader_hint":"Look for neutral language that identifies the source, dispute, and materiality. Repetition of “no injury” without qualification fails even if another section mentions that the recording is unavailable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The California analysis applies traceability to the material closure fact by assessing whether its source, actor, event time, evidentiary support, and reliance in N-114 can be reconstructed.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"California portion of the jurisdiction comparison.","grader_hint":"The analysis must apply the control to the disputed statement and closure chain. A generic statement that California requires good records is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Nevada analysis applies minimization by limiting retained health detail to what is necessary to document the dispute, decision, and audit trail, and by avoiding unnecessary repetition or embellishment of the client’s alleged condition.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Nevada portion of the jurisdiction comparison and the detail actually retained elsewhere in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Assess both stated reasoning and implementation. A claim of minimization is not sufficient if the workbook reproduces unnecessary sensitive narrative or invents additional clinical detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The cross-jurisdiction conclusion reconciles rather than chooses between the controls: it retains concise provenance and the existence and materiality of the dispute for traceability while withholding unsupported or unnecessary health detail.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Integrated California–Nevada conclusion and corresponding register treatment.","grader_hint":"Look for one workable case-level approach that satisfies both controls. Treating either traceability or minimization as eliminating the other does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The closure-control analysis shows that N-114 relied on the disputed no-injury statement, that the statement was neither supported nor recorded as unresolved, and that the resulting corrected classification is status “Open” with disposition “Inconclusive.”","weight":7.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Closure analysis, decision, and normalized label fields.","grader_hint":"Verify the reasoning chain and exact end-state vocabulary. The legacy label may remain visible as source data, but it cannot remain the operative corrected classification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook supports the transition period and end state by retaining original LegacyContact and CaseHub provenance, recognizing dual-system records through 15 May, and supplying canonical status and disposition labels suitable after CaseHub became sole system of record on 16 May.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Register lineage, label mapping, and transition notes.","grader_hint":"The workbook must not erase legacy terminology or perpetuate it as the only future-facing label. Check that both original and canonical representations are intelligible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook draws a practical must/should boundary: correcting the evidence, figures, classification, and closure decision is mandatory for Friday, while later recording retrieval, date verification, and fuller revalidation are identified as advisable follow-up that does not postpone the present recommendation.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Decision conditions, control classification, and follow-up treatment.","grader_hint":"Accept different concise presentation formats, but the obligatory corrections and prudent later work must be clearly distinguished. The decision cannot be made conditional on obtaining the recording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The unavailable call recording and limits of the same-day supervisory note are disclosed, and the workbook does not claim to know the recording’s contents or use the note as confirmation of the disputed wording.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Limitations, evidence assessment, and N-112 treatment.","grader_hint":"Check that the note is used only to confirm occurrence and participants. Any assertion that it corroborates “no injury” fails this criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The change log substantively records the correction of period logic, duplicate treatment, malformed-date treatment, label normalization, treatment of the disputed statement, recalculated figures, and changed closure conclusion.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook change log.","grader_hint":"The log must let a reviewer understand what changed from the draft and why. A generic entry such as “data corrected” is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook remains confined to the supplied complaint and frozen snapshot and does not invent a replacement date, recording content, statutory deadline, outside contact volume, unrelated rate, financial impact, or broader complaint-management procedure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Entire workbook.","grader_hint":"Review narrative, tables, notes, and formulas for unsupported facts or procedural expansion. Necessary case-specific follow-up controls do not constitute a prohibited redesign."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is practical for peer review and reuse: the decision and key figures are easy to locate, register entries remain editable and auditable, labels and exceptions are intelligible, and visual treatment does not obscure disputed or excluded evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and editable cell structure.","grader_hint":"Inspect the workbook visually and interact with the register. Award credit only if a subject-matter reviewer could validate the recommendation without asking the author to decode the structure."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Ambergate Institute provides compliance oversight for Heronbank Logistics’ cross-border home-health coordination service. A medical and health services manager must correct a single complaint assessment before a peer reviewer makes a time-sensitive closure decision.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling event dates against migration creation dates and duplicate lineage","Applying competing California traceability and Nevada minimization controls to one disputed health detail","Separating mandatory closure corrections from advisable revalidation while the key recording is unavailable","Representing both a transition-era legacy practice and the canonical end state","Maintaining agreement among the decision narrative, period metrics, evidence register, and change log"],"authoring_plan":{"task_design":{"solver_instance":"A medical and health services manager must reconcile a fixed eight-entry complaint record, compare two jurisdiction-specific controls, and issue one closure recommendation in a single editable workbook.","behavior_specification":"The solver should distinguish source-event time from migration-record creation time, preserve excluded records for auditability, normalize transition-era labels, avoid elevating disputed health information to fact, and make a present decision despite an unavailable recording.","intended_verdict":"The existing closure is not valid and the complaint should be reopened. The corrected end-state classification is status Open and disposition Inconclusive because N-114 relied on a disputed material assertion that was not supported or expressly treated as unresolved."},"required_case_imperfections":["M-880 duplicates L-880 by source reference and event time but has a 2 April CaseHub creation date.","M-881 duplicates L-881 by source reference and event time but has a 2 April CaseHub creation date.","N-113 contains the impossible raw date 31/04/2026 14:20 and must remain visible without being assigned to a period.","N-112 contains a material no-injury statement disputed by the client; the call occurrence and participants are corroborated, but the wording is not.","N-114 uses a legacy combined label and relies on the disputed statement without noting the dispute.","The recording needed for full revalidation is unavailable before the operational deadline.","The source-system and label practices are mid-transition, requiring both legacy traceability and an end-state representation."],"gold_relationships":["A valid unique contact is counted once by the date on which the interaction occurred, not by a migration or record-creation date.","L-880, L-881, and L-882 are valid unique Q1 contacts.","M-880 and M-881 are retained as audit records but contribute zero additional contacts because they are migration copies of L-880 and L-881.","N-112 and N-114 are valid unique Q2 contacts.","N-113 contributes to neither period because its date is impossible and no replacement date is supported.","The corrected totals are Q1 3, Q2 2, total 5, absolute change -1, and percentage change ((2-3)/3)*100 = -33.333..., displayed as -33.3%.","The draft’s apparent increase results from counting migration creation dates, duplicates, and the malformed entry; it is not evidence of an operating trend.","The California control makes concise provenance, dispute status, and reliance in closure necessary to retain.","The Nevada control supports retaining only a neutral statement that a material assertion is disputed, along with its provenance and decision relevance, rather than unnecessary or unsupported health detail.","The internal closure control fails because the disputed assertion influenced N-114, was not supported, and was not expressly treated as unresolved.","The unavailable recording limits full revalidation but does not prevent a decision that the existing closure was improper.","Mandatory pre-Friday work consists of correcting the evidence treatment, metrics, canonical classification, and closure conclusion. Recording retrieval, malformed-date verification, and fuller revalidation are prudent later actions and must not make the decision conditional.","Legacy source labels remain visible for lineage, while the operative normalized outcome is Open and Inconclusive."],"required_vocabulary_and_source":{"request_supplied_terms":["Open","Closed","Substantiated","Unsubstantiated","Inconclusive","Closed—resolved","LegacyContact","CaseHub"],"usage":"The gold should preserve the original legacy label as evidence and use the supplied canonical status and disposition vocabulary for the corrected result."},"gold_quality_expectations":["Every supplied identifier remains independently traceable even when excluded from a count.","The decision-facing portion gives one recommendation and finishes on that decision rather than on future actions.","The evidence register allows recalculation of the displayed figures and makes duplicate, invalid-date, disputed-evidence, and label-mapping decisions visible.","The change log identifies each substantive correction and its effect on the assessment.","The workbook remains an assessment package and evidence register rather than becoming a new complaint procedure.","The rendered workbook is suitable for Friday peer review and the underlying register remains editable."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"complaint_closure_assessment","filename":"heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A decision-facing corrected compliance assessment, editable evidence register, jurisdiction comparison, and change log for complaint HL-26-0327.","required":true,"constraints":["Create exactly one deliverable at the top level of the working directory using the specified filename.","Include a decision-facing assessment, supporting evidence register, California–Nevada comparison, and substantive change log within the workbook.","Use only the case facts and frozen requirements stated in the request.","Do not expand the workbook into a redesigned complaint-management procedure.","The workbook must remain readable, navigable, and editable in standard spreadsheet software."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"medical_health_services_managers","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference workbook must be independently reviewed by one healthcare compliance operations specialist and one spreadsheet-quality reviewer. Reviewers should recalculate the period metrics from the register, verify the closure-control reasoning, and inspect the rendered workbook for decision usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The California and Nevada controls are a synthetic frozen requirements snapshot supplied in the request rather than a representation of all live law.","The call recording is intentionally unavailable, so neither the gold nor a solver submission can verify its contents.","The case contains no direct client identifier or clinical record beyond the disputed no-injury statement."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:26:07+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:26:07+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:26:07+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:26:07+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/0bb0f5236c32c35a","declared_deliverables":["heronbank_complaint_closure_assessment.xlsx"]};
